WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.180
A caterpillar spends
its days eating leaves.

2
00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:06.120
It is little more than a mouth on legs.

3
00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:09.490
Yet of every 100 units of energy it eats,

4
00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:12.700
only about 15 become new caterpillar.

5
00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:17.600
And when a bird eats the caterpillar,
those 15 are all the bird can get.

6
00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:20.000
So where does the rest of the leaf go?

7
00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:23.350
Why does so little of it
end up as caterpillar?

8
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:28.580
In this mission, you'll see how plants
capture and store energy in the first place.

9
00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:31.930
Then you'll follow a consumer's
food from the first bite,

10
00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:35.110
and track where every
unit of energy ends up.

11
00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:39.890
Your mission: explain why so little
of a leaf ever becomes caterpillar.
